		"notes": "\n\t<p><i>Purple, velvet-covered moth with 15-foot wide violet wings. Dwellers in shadow and deep, dark places.</i></p>\n\t<p></p>\n\t<p><strong>AC</strong> 11, <strong>HP</strong> 9, <strong>ATK</strong> 1 proboscis +1 (1d4) or implant, <strong>MV</strong> near (fly), <strong>S</strong> +0, <strong>D</strong> +1, <strong>C</strong> +0, <strong>I</strong> -3, <strong>W</strong> +0, <strong>Ch</strong> -3, <strong>AL</strong> N, <strong>LV</strong> 2</p><p></p>\n\t<p><strong>Implant</strong>. Lay eggs inside helpless mortal. CON 15+ or 1d4 CON damage (cannot heal while ill). Repeat check once per day; ends on success. Die at 0 CON, spawning 1d4 tenebrous worms which burst from the corpse and devour it.</p><p></p><p><strong>Stupefy</strong>. Any creature who looks directly at gloomwing, CHA 15+ or stupefied for 1 round.</p><p></p>\n\t<p><i>Shadowfinder Complete Bestiary</i></p>",
